=== Prompt ===
Who is Lara Croft?

=== Response ===
Lara Croft is a fictional character and the protagonist of the popular video game series 'Tomb Raider.' She was created by Toby Gard and first appeared in the 1996 game 'Tomb Raider,' developed by Core Design and published by Eidos Interactive.

Lara Croft is an English archaeologist, adventurer, and explorer who goes on expeditions to uncover lost artifacts and treasures from ancient civilizations. She is known for her intelligence, athleticism, and bravery. Lara is also skilled in combat, martial arts, and survival skills, making her a formidable opponent in various challenging situations.

Throughout the series, Lara has undergone several transformations, evolving from a more timid and inexperienced character in the early games to a more confident and assertive one in the later titles. The character has been portrayed by several actresses in various film adaptations, including Angelina Jolie in the 2001 movie 'Lara Croft: Tomb Raider' and Alicia Vikander in the 2018 film 'Tomb Raider.'

Lara Croft has become an iconic figure in the world of gaming and popular culture, inspiring numerous fans worldwide with her adventurous spirit and determination to uncover the secrets of the past.

